<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  CATHEDRAL_ROACH_THINKTREE_GAP_1 — the cathedral roach's own main think tree.

  WHY A WHOLE TREE AND NOT AN insertTag SUBTREE: RUT_CathedralRoach is
  ParentName="BaseMechanoidWalker", so its inherited tree is vanilla
  "Mechanoid" (Defs/Core/ThinkTreeDefs/Mechanoid.xml). That tree carries NO
  insertTag of any kind - the Animal_PreMain hook RM_ThinkTree_VerminBehaviors
  rides (mandrake.rm.creaturebehaviors) has nothing to attach to, so
  RM_ThinkNode_EatCleanable (wired via the ThingDef's own
  RM_EatCleanableExtension modExtension) was never reachable: the roach
  spawned, wandered, and never cleaned anything. Same root cause, same fix
  shape as RUT_LivingBolt (RustCathedralHum/Defs/ThinkTreeDefs/
  RUT_ThinkTree_LivingBolt.xml) - a dedicated tree scoped to exactly one race,
  built for what this creature actually needs rather than a lord/overseer
  combat tree it has no use for.

  RUT_ScarRoach, the organic Scarlands sibling, does NOT have this bug:
  ParentName="AnimalThingBase" inherits vanilla "Animal", which DOES carry
  Animal_PreMain, so its EatCleanable node already reaches its think tree
  through the normal route. This file exists only for the mechanoid side.

  NO HUM WIRING (kit spec, rust_cathedral_kit_spec.md §6, owner ruling
  2026-09-07, verbatim on the item): "no attitude input, no freeze/scatter
  tell... roach think trees never reference RM_MapComponent_BiomeAttitude."
  Unlike RUT_ThinkTree_LivingBolt, this tree has no
  RM_ThinkNode_ConditionalAttitudeBand freeze and no RM_JobGiver_ResonantDance
  - the roaches are fauna, not instrumentation.

  ORDER: Despawned/Downed (vanilla, every tree) - QueuedJob (finish whatever
  is in progress) - EatCleanable (the point of the creature) - tagged Idle
  wander (vanilla JobGiver_WanderAnywhere, the graceful-degradation floor:
  RM_ThinkNode_EatCleanable returns no job for any race lacking its
  extension or when nothing cleanable is in range, and the roach is then an
  ordinary wandering mechanoid critter) - IdleError (vanilla backstop).
-->
<Defs>

  <ThinkTreeDef>
    <defName>RUT_ThinkTree_CathedralRoach</defName>
    <thinkRoot Class="ThinkNode_Priority">
      <subNodes>

        <li Class="ThinkNode_Subtree">
          <treeDef>Despawned</treeDef>
        </li>

        <li Class="ThinkNode_Subtree">
          <treeDef>Downed</treeDef>
        </li>

        <li Class="ThinkNode_QueuedJob" />

        <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_ThinkNode_EatCleanable" />

        <li Class="ThinkNode_Tagger">
          <tagToGive>Idle</tagToGive>
          <subNodes>
            <li Class="JobGiver_WanderAnywhere">
              <maxDanger>Deadly</maxDanger>
            </li>
          </subNodes>
        </li>

        <li Class="JobGiver_IdleError" />

      </subNodes>
    </thinkRoot>
  </ThinkTreeDef>

</Defs>
